{
  "_comment": "Per target language (slice 07 section 7): the romanization scheme (null for Latin-script targets, \"unspecified\" until a contributor names one), the stress kind (lexical: one capital syllable per word of two or more syllables; none: all lowercase; a target with no entry is \"unknown\": either shape), the tone digit range or null, and the marks native_vocalized may add. Looked up by the full tag, then by the language when the tag names no script; a target with no entry gets no scheme when its script is Latin and \"unspecified\" otherwise. schemes holds the description the prompt carries for each scheme. Mandarin-style targets (neutral_tone: true) may leave the neutral syllable without a digit; others need a digit on every syllable. stress_marked targets put U+0301 in native_vocalized, checked against the capital syllable by counting vowel_letters.",
  "schemes": {
    "kotiko-bgn-pcgn-simple": "Kotiko's simplified BGN/PCGN: а a, б b, в v, г g, д d, е e (ye at the start of a word and after a vowel, ъ or ь), ё yo, ж zh, з z, и i, й y, к k, л l, м m, н n, о o, п p, р r, с s, т t, у u, ф f, х kh, ц ts, ч ch, ш sh, щ shch, ы y, э e, ю yu, я ya; ъ and ь dropped; no stress marks, dots or apostrophes (пожалуйста pozhaluysta)",
    "ukrainian-national-2010": "the Ukrainian national transliteration of 2010 (дякую dyakuyu)",
    "belarusian-national-2007": "the Belarusian national system of 2007 (дзякуй dziakuj)",
    "bulgarian-streamlined-2009": "the Bulgarian Streamlined System of 2009 (благодаря blagodarya)",
    "serbian-latin": "the Serbian Latin alphabet (хвала hvala)",
    "pinyin-tone-marks": "Hanyu Pinyin with tone marks and dictionary tones (no tone sandhi), the syllables of one word written together (谢谢 xièxie, 你好 nǐ hǎo)",
    "jyutping": "Jyutping with tone digits (多謝 do1 ze6)",
    "hepburn-modified": "modified Hepburn of the kana reading, macrons for long vowels (ありがとう arigatō, 好き suki)",
    "revised-romanization-2000": "the Revised Romanization of Korean (감사합니다 gamsahamnida)",
    "ala-lc-simplified": "ALA-LC without dots and macrons, ʿayn and hamza as an apostrophe, the short vowels of Modern Standard Arabic written out (شكرا shukran, مرحبا marhaban)",
    "hebrew-academy-2006": "the Academy of the Hebrew Language's simplified rules of 2006 (תודה toda)",
    "elot-743": "ELOT 743 (ευχαριστώ efcharistó)",
    "hunterian": "Hunterian (धन्यवाद dhanyavad)",
    "rtgs": "the Royal Thai General System (ขอบคุณ khop khun)",
    "georgian-national-2002": "the Georgian national system of 2002 (მადლობა madloba)"
  },
